    "article_summary": "The article describes a dual photochemical/nickel-mediated decarboxylative cross-coupling strategy for C(sp3)-C(sp2) bond formation. The method utilizes Hantzsch ester (HE) as a dual-purpose organic photoreductant that both forms an electron donor-acceptor (EDA) complex with redox-active esters to generate alkyl radicals and restores the active Ni(0) catalyst via single-electron transfer (SET), eliminating the need for precious metal photocatalysts or stoichiometric metal reductants.",
